tests:
Extend test_never_more_than_one_probe_window_in_flight (line 18273) and add proptest_attribution_rules: random sequences of 805, bare resets on random slots with random recent_dials masks, sibling dialled, sibling left, watched self-redial and polls. Assert:
- at most one window;
- at most one grant per step;
- caps respected;
- a Failed* outcome only when its rule matches (805, watched close, corroborated mask excluding the closer and the burst, deadline, deferral cap, watched idle);
- no ProbePassed or ReleasePassed while suspect_mask!=0 or now<settle_until.

Source pins:
- the Disconnected arm contains overflow_episode_note_disconnect(code, self.slot.global_index, now);
- the BeginDial arm calls overflow_note_dial_begin;
- the DialSucceeded arm calls overflow_episode_note_dial_succeeded;
- park() calls the non-805 hook after the respawn return;
- OVERFLOW_SUSPECT_MASK is stored inside the overflow_episode_step lock block;
- the OverflowEpisode/OverflowEpisodes region contains no Vec, Box, String, format! or to_string. This replaces the false claim that DHAT covers the supervisor.
